WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.072
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:08.294
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.594 --> 00:00:14.241
Unit five: Mind and Body. In this unit, you will talk about health habits and past advice.

4
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:16.181
sedentary.

5
00:00:16.881 --> 00:00:20.228
sedentary means involving a lot of sitting and little exercise.

6
00:00:20.528 --> 00:00:23.456
Office workers often have a sedentary lifestyle.

7
00:00:24.156 --> 00:00:26.483
Your turn. Say: sedentary.

8
00:00:29.183 --> 00:00:30.231
sedentary.

9
00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:32.311
stress relief.

10
00:00:33.011 --> 00:00:36.252
stress relief means something that reduces worry and pressure.

11
00:00:36.552 --> 00:00:38.506
Swimming is my favourite stress relief.

12
00:00:39.206 --> 00:00:41.649
Your turn. Say: stress relief.

13
00:00:44.349 --> 00:00:45.710
stress relief.

14
00:00:46.717 --> 00:00:48.112
sleep deprivation.

15
00:00:48.812 --> 00:00:51.602
sleep deprivation means not getting enough sleep.

16
00:00:51.902 --> 00:00:54.064
Sleep deprivation affects your memory.

17
00:00:54.764 --> 00:00:57.602
Your turn. Say: sleep deprivation.

18
00:01:00.302 --> 00:01:01.767
sleep deprivation.

19
00:01:02.783 --> 00:01:03.715
therapist.

20
00:01:04.415 --> 00:01:08.237
therapist means a person trained to help with mental or physical problems.

21
00:01:08.537 --> 00:01:11.013
Talking to a therapist helped her through a hard year.

22
00:01:11.713 --> 00:01:13.854
Your turn. Say: therapist.

23
00:01:16.554 --> 00:01:17.578
therapist.

24
00:01:18.583 --> 00:01:19.468
wellness.

25
00:01:20.168 --> 00:01:22.516
wellness means being healthy in body and mind.

26
00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:25.872
The company offers wellness classes on Fridays.

27
00:01:26.572 --> 00:01:28.934
Your turn. Say: wellness.

28
00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:32.670
wellness.

29
00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:34.951
posture problems.

30
00:01:35.651 --> 00:01:39.892
posture problems means pain or difficulty caused by sitting or standing badly.

31
00:01:40.192 --> 00:01:43.317
Many students have posture problems from using phones.

32
00:01:44.017 --> 00:01:46.623
Your turn. Say: posture problems.

33
00:01:49.323 --> 00:01:50.731
posture problems.

34
00:01:51.717 --> 00:01:52.927
meditation app.

35
00:01:53.627 --> 00:01:57.379
meditation app means a phone application that guides you through meditation.

36
00:01:57.679 --> 00:01:59.865
I use a meditation app before bed.

37
00:02:00.565 --> 00:02:03.020
Your turn. Say: meditation app.

38
00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.057
meditation app.

39
00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:09.202
physiotherapy.

40
00:02:09.902 --> 00:02:13.806
physiotherapy means treatment for injuries using exercise and massage.

41
00:02:14.106 --> 00:02:17.162
After the accident, he needed physiotherapy for months.

42
00:02:17.862 --> 00:02:20.746
Your turn. Say: physiotherapy.

43
00:02:23.446 --> 00:02:24.668
physiotherapy.

44
00:02:25.683 --> 00:02:27.567
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:27.867 --> 00:02:30.040
My back has been hurting for weeks.

46
00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:34.734
You should have seen a doctor earlier. Do you have posture problems?

47
00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:39.074
Probably. My job is completely sedentary.

48
00:02:40.383 --> 00:02:43.941
You ought to have taken more breaks. Have you tried physiotherapy?

49
00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:49.223
Not yet, but my therapist suggested a meditation app for stress relief.

50
00:02:50.517 --> 00:02:53.355
Good. Wellness is about both mind and body.

51
00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:58.716
Grammar focus: Modals of advice and obligation (past).

52
00:02:59.016 --> 00:03:02.362
Use should have or ought to have to criticise or regret past actions.

53
00:03:02.662 --> 00:03:07.808
Use had to for past obligation, and needn't have for something unnecessary that you did.

54
00:03:08.108 --> 00:03:11.838
For example: You should have rested more, and you needn't have bought medicine.

55
00:03:12.138 --> 00:03:17.066
Needn't have done means you did it, but it wasn't necessary. Didn't need to usually means you didn't do it.

56
00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:20.853
Now read and listen. The Hidden Cost of Sitting.

57
00:03:21.153 --> 00:03:24.720
Many office workers spend more than nine hours a day sitting down.

58
00:03:26.017 --> 00:03:29.723
Doctors warn that a sedentary lifestyle can be as harmful as smoking.

59
00:03:31.017 --> 00:03:34.676
Posture problems and back pain are now common even among young people.

60
00:03:35.983 --> 00:03:39.585
Experts say we should have been taking short walking breaks every hour.

61
00:03:40.883 --> 00:03:45.774
Combined with good sleep and stress relief, small movements improve overall wellness.

62
00:03:47.083 --> 00:03:49.527
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:49.827 --> 00:03:51.664
Not getting enough sleep is blank.

64
00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:55.768
A, sleep deprivation. B, wellness. C, stress relief.

65
00:03:59.783 --> 00:04:02.596
The answer is A: sleep deprivation.

66
00:04:04.083 --> 00:04:07.014
You look tired. You blank gone to bed earlier.

67
00:04:07.314 --> 00:04:10.817
A, should have. B, must. C, had to.

68
00:04:14.817 --> 00:04:16.805
The answer is A: should have.

69
00:04:18.317 --> 00:04:20.873
I blank work late yesterday because of a deadline.

70
00:04:21.173 --> 00:04:24.804
A, should have. B, had to. C, needn't have.

71
00:04:28.817 --> 00:04:30.561
The answer is B: had to.

72
00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:35.164
Treatment for injuries using exercise and massage is blank.

73
00:04:35.464 --> 00:04:39.803
A, physiotherapy. B, meditation app. C, therapist.

74
00:04:43.817 --> 00:04:46.466
The answer is A: physiotherapy.

75
00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:52.272
According to the text, a sedentary lifestyle can be as harmful as blank.

76
00:04:52.572 --> 00:04:55.749
A, coffee. B, smoking. C, sport.

77
00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:01.912
The answer is B: smoking.

78
00:05:03.417 --> 00:05:07.602
Now it's your turn to speak. What health advice do you wish you had followed earlier?

79
00:05:12.902 --> 00:05:19.014
I should have exercised more at university. I sat at my desk all day and developed posture problems.

80
00:05:19.314 --> 00:05:20.884
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:21.883 --> 00:05:26.881
Great work today! You learned eight new words and modals of advice and obligation (past).

82
00:05:27.181 --> 00:05:30.634
Today's value is healthy body. Move your body every day.

83
00:05:30.934 --> 00:05:33.285
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

84
00:05:33.585 --> 00:05:36.237
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

